     "result_text_tail": "ok at the slides as images. LibreOffice isn't installed and the sandbox blocks scripting Keynote, so I relied on the render's layout checks and a read of the slide text. Please flip through the deck in PowerPoint or Keynote before it goes out.\n\n**Choices I made in your place:**\n- I built the long version (43 slides, structured around an issue tree), because this is a CEO decision with several open questions behind it.\n- The audience is the CEO and executive team deciding at January 2027 planning.\n- The deck uses only the briefing pack; there was no web research.\n- Out of scope: Core price changes, building our own AI model, and hiring beyond the 60 engineers.\n- **Assumption to confirm with engineering:** if the mobile rewrite goes first, Copilot ships two quarters later (Q4 2027), when the 14 engineers are free. The pack doesn't give the rewrite's own schedule.\n- I set the allowance at its break-even point, about 1,330 requests per seat a month, where AI costs equal the $12 seat price. The final number should come from the price test.\n- The \"ARR at risk\" figures are upper bounds on both sides: they assume each fix removes all the churn or lost deals of its kind.\n\nYou could next switch the theme (crimson, forest, mono, vivid, slate or terracotta) or put the Q4 2026 win-rate reading into the deck once it's in.\n\nFiles are in `./deliverable/`:\n- brightwork-copilot.pptx\n- brightwork-copilot-sources.xlsx\n- brightwork-copilot.json (the spec; edit it and re-render to change the deck)"
    }
